## Structure

```
beauty-bliss-tracker/
├── client/                     # Vite React SPA
│   ├── index.html
│   └── src/
│       ├── main.tsx            # Entry: App, QueryClient, Toaster
│       ├── App.tsx             # AuthProvider + wouter hash routes
│       ├── index.css           # Tailwind + CSS variables (rose accent)
│       ├── pages/
│       │   ├── login.tsx       # PIN login
│       │   ├── ba-entry.tsx    # Daily sales entry
│       │   ├── ba-dashboard.tsx
│       │   ├── dashboard.tsx   # Management shell/nav
│       │   ├── dashboard/      # management-dashboard, brand-dashboard,
│       │   │                   # promotions, incentive-tracking,
│       │   │                   # pos-reconciliation, settings
│       │   └── not-found.tsx
│       ├── components/
│       │   ├── ui/             # shadcn primitives — regenerate via CLI only
│       │   └── *.tsx           # App-specific components
│       ├── hooks/
│       └── lib/                # queryClient, utils (cn), export helpers
├── server/
│   ├── index.ts                # Bootstrap; PORT from env; session; Vite or static
│   ├── routes.ts               # ALL API routes under /api/*
│   ├── storage.ts              # IStorage + PgStorage + MemStorage; `storage` singleton
│   ├── vite.ts                 # Dev Vite middleware
│   └── static.ts               # Prod static from dist/public
├── shared/
│   ├── schema.ts               # SINGLE SOURCE OF TRUTH (Drizzle + Zod + types)
│   └── deductionAllocation.ts
├── script/build.ts
├── drizzle.config.ts
├── tailwind.config.ts
├── vite.config.ts
└── tsconfig.json
```

**Path aliases (client and server):**
- `@/*` → `client/src/*`
- `@shared/*` → `shared/*`
- `@assets` → `attached_assets`

**Routing (after login):**
- `ba` / `part_time` → `/` (BA entry), `/my-dashboard`. Redirect `/dashboard/*` to `/`.
- `management` → `/` plus `/dashboard` and sub-pages.

---

## Conventions

### TypeScript
- Strict mode always on. No `any` unless annotated with `// eslint-disable` and a reason.
- Prefer `type` for props/DTOs; `interface` only for extendable contracts (`IStorage`).
- Use `import type { ... }` for type-only imports.
- ESM only (`import`/`export`). No CommonJS `require` in source files.
- TypeScript only in `client/src` and `server/` — no `.jsx` / `.js`.

### Schema & types
- Both sides import from `@shared/schema`. Never copy-paste entity shapes.
- Legacy `counters` / `counterBrands` stay for backward compatibility. New work uses `posLocations`, `users`, `userPosAssignments`, `brandPosAvailability`.

### React (client)
- Functional components only. Pages: named function + default export, e.g. `export default function BAEntry() { ... }`.
- Server state → TanStack Query (`useQuery`, `useMutation`). Local UI state → `useState`. Do not put server data in extra Context except the existing `AuthContext` in `App.tsx`.
- Query keys: array form starting with the resource path, e.g. `['/api/sales', { date }]`. Reuse the same shape for invalidation.
- Forms: `react-hook-form` + `zodResolver` bound to the matching `@shared/schema` Zod schema.
- Routing: wouter (`useLocation`, `Link`, `Route`, `Switch`, `Redirect`, hash location). Never add react-router.
- Never mutate props or query cache data in place. Return new objects; update via `queryClient.setQueryData` / `invalidateQueries`.
- No `useEffect` for data fetching — use TanStack Query. Auth session check on mount in `AuthProvider` is the existing exception.
- No `window` / `document` access outside components; wrap in `useEffect` when unavoidable.
- Use `useAuth()` from `App.tsx` for the current user. Do not invent a second auth store.
- API calls must send `credentials: "same-origin"` so the session cookie is included (already set in `queryClient.ts`).

### UI & styling
- Use existing shadcn/ui from `client/src/components/ui/` before building new ones.
- **Do not hand-edit `components/ui/`** — regenerate via the shadcn CLI.
- Tailwind utilities only. Compose classes with `cn()` from `@/lib/utils`.
- Keep the rose/blush accent (`340 65% 47%`) on a warm white theme. Do not add new accent colors without approval.
- Accessible defaults: keyboard-navigable, WCAG AA contrast, `aria-*` where Radix does not cover it.
- No `alert()` / `confirm()` — use shadcn `Dialog` / `AlertDialog` and `useToast`.

### Server / API
- Register every route in `server/routes.ts` under `/api/*`.
- Validate every request body with the matching Zod schema from `@shared/schema`. Reject with 400 on failure.
- Use the exported `storage` singleton for all data access. Do not touch Maps / SQL from routes.
- Never hardcode a port — `process.env.PORT` with a dev fallback. Never call `app.listen` outside `server/index.ts`.
- Keep handlers thin: parse → validate → auth check → delegate to `storage` → respond. Multi-entity logic belongs in `storage.ts`.
- Session middleware is wired in `server/index.ts` **after** storage init (so the `session` table exists for `connect-pg-simple`).

### Auth (current behavior)
- Login: `POST /api/auth/login` (username + PIN). Logout: `POST /api/auth/logout`. Session: `GET /api/auth/me`. PIN change: `POST /api/auth/change-pin`.
- `requireAuth`: session must have `userId`.
- `requireManagement`: session role must be `management`.
- Default: GET routes → `requireAuth`; mutating routes → `requireManagement`, unless a BA must write (e.g. their own sales entry).
- Hash PINs with `bcryptjs` before storing. Never return the PIN hash to the client.
- BA / part-time users only see assigned POS locations. Brands are filtered by `brandPosAvailability` for the selected POS.

### Storage
- `IStorage` is the contract. Add new methods to the interface first, then implement on **both** `PgStorage` and `MemStorage`.
- `storage` is `PgStorage` when `DATABASE_URL` is set, otherwise `MemStorage`.
- Do not leak Mem-specific behavior (sync returns) into callers. Every storage method returns a `Promise`.

### CSV / external data
- Parse with `csv-parse/sync` using `columns: true, skip_empty_lines: true, relax_column_count: true, trim: true`.
- Map external brand codes through `BRAND_CODE_MAP` in `server/routes.ts`. Do not scatter magic strings.
- Sync endpoints must be idempotent: upsert on a stable natural key (e.g. `PromotionID`), never blind-insert.

### Naming
- Components: `PascalCase.tsx`. Hooks: `use-kebab-case.ts`. Utilities: `kebab-case.ts`.
- One default-exported component per page file; co-locate small helpers.

### Git / deploy
- Do not commit `node_modules/`, `dist/`, `.env`, or `*.db-shm` / `*.db-wal`.
- Railway sets `NODE_ENV=production`. Do not set `PORT` manually in Railway variables.
- Client output: `dist/public/`. Server output: `dist/index.cjs`. Both from `npm run build`.
- Run `npm run check` (tsc) before every commit — zero TypeScript errors is the merge bar.

### Testing (when adding checks)
- Any new API route needs at least one happy-path and one validation-failure check.

---

## Guardrails

- Do not remove login or open `/` and `/dashboard/*` to the public.
- Do not protect these server-to-server promotion endpoints unless asked: `POST /api/promotions/push` and the related no-auth promotion lookup/delete-by-source-id routes already in `routes.ts`.
- Do not introduce a new state manager. TanStack Query + local state + existing `AuthContext` is enough.
- Do not hardcode counter names, brand names, POS names, or promotion types — they are user-editable data in `storage`.
- No global mutable singletons other than `storage` and `queryClient`.
- Never mutate global state directly — go through setters, mutations, or `storage` methods.
- Keep `counters` / `counterBrands` working if you touch them; prefer POS location APIs for new features.
- After dependency changes: `npm install` and commit the updated `package-lock.json`.
